{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Basics on PHP, Hypertext Preprocessor", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "You can use these words to talk about PHP.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of  work contexts.   Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of  work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "open-source", "type": "name"}, {"content": "free software and available to anyone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: PHP is an open-source scripting language.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "intricate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "complicated and hard to understand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: PHP must be very intricate to use.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "freak out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get angry ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't freak out, Sophie. I believe you should use PHP. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "convince ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to persuade someone about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Okay, you convinced me; I'm going to use PHP, but my computer uses Linux, can it run it? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "versatile ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "handy and useful for several purposes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Data can be opened, read, written, deleted, collected and even closed. It is very versatile. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le02ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look for information about how PHP works.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a brochure to explain PHP. . ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your brochure with the rest of your class. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I know what PHP is. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about the capabilities of PHP.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give reasons to use PHP. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Questions Within Sentences: How to - Where to - What to", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Sometimes, you want to ask a question inside a negative or affirmative sentence, in those cases, we use <strong>how to, where to</strong>, and <strong>what to</strong>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "To ask questions within a negative or affirmative sentence, follow this structure: </br></br>  Sentence +<b> how to / what to / where to </b>+ verb + complement </br></br> <i> Examples:</br> I don't need to ask <b>how to use</b> PHP, I have a master.</br> Let me know <b>where to go</b>.</br> I don't know <b>what to do</b> with those programming languages.</i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Lucas! I don't know what to do! I need to choose between using JavaScript or using PHP. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you want to know how to control user access, PHP is the best alternative.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Passive of Modal Verbs: Can", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use the <b>passive voice</b> when we want to focus the attention on the object or action and not on the person who does it. <br></br> <b>Passive voice </b>can be used anytime; we are going to focus on its use along the modal verb <b>can</b> this time.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<strong>Can</strong> shares similar uses with <strong>may</strong> and <strong>might;</strong> the last two are more formal. Plus, <strong>can</strong> is used to express possibility, permission or ability. </br></br>  Look at the following structure: <br></br><center> Subject + <b>can be </b>+ <b>verb in past participle</b> + complement</br></br> </center> Examples</br><i> This software <strong>can be modified</strong> by the experts. </br> This item <strong>can only be bought</strong> in the online store.</i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Beginners have it because it can be used easily, right? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "With all of that\u2026 it can be used to generate dynamic page content! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Data can be opened, read, written, deleted, collected and even closed. It is very versatile.", "type": "example"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can say what PHP is.   ", "type": "Lear