images": [{"time": "100", "text": "<strong>Sophie:</strong> Lucas! I don't know what to do! I need to choose between using JavaScript and using PHP, but my knowledge on PHP is as deep as a glass of water.</br>\n<strong>Lucas:</strong> Don't freak out, Sophie. I believe you should use PHP. </br>\n<strong>Sophie:</strong> Do you know how to use it?<br>\n<strong>Lucas:</strong>  Yes. I can tell you how to manage it. <br>\n<strong>Sophie:</strong> Sure! I know that WordPress uses PHP, and I understand that it is the biggest blogging system; indeed, I think PHP must be very intricate to use. </br>", "image": "enpe7n6le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "36000", "text": "<strong>Lucas:</strong> It isn't, actually; let me explain. PHP stands for Hypertext Preprocessor; it is a widely used open-source scripting language. It's free to use, and the best thing, it is executed on the server. It is deep enough to run on Facebook! </br>\n<strong>Sophie:</strong> Wait a minute, I've heard of it! Beginners usually start with this one because it can be handled easily, right? </br>\n<strong>Lucas:</strong> That's true. Many people use it because it can contain text, HTML, CSS, PHP code and JavaScript. </br>\n<strong>Sophie:</strong> With all those features, I guess it can be used to generate dynamic page content! </br>\n<strong>Lucas:</strong> Correct. Data can be opened, read, written, deleted, collected and even closed. PHP is quite versatile. </br>", "image": "enpe7n6le02ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "91000", "text": "<strong>Sophie:</strong> Can it send and receive cookies? </br>\n<strong>Lucas:</strong> That and even more! You can modify the database and encrypt data. If you want to know how to control user access, PHP is the best alternative. </br>\n<strong>Sophie:</strong> Okay, you convinced me; I'm going to use PHP, but my computer uses Linux, can it run PHP? </br>\n<strong>Lucas:</strong> Of course, it runs on many Operating systems, including Windows and even Mac Os X. It is also compatible with Apache and IIS.</br>\n<strong>Sophie:</strong> Lucas, you seem very knowledgeable about PHP.</br>\n<strong>Lucas:</strong> Yes! Since I discovered it, it has made my job much easier. Then, if you want, I can show you how to operate other systems with PHP.", "image": "enpe7n6le02ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n6le02ob01re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}